{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Does he not… equate.</b> A gezerah shavah [ verbal analogy], as in 'and a woman of strife is compared' (Proverbs 27:15)." "<b>Nigella.</b> It is like cumin but finer than it, and it is black." "<b>Row.</b> Some say 'the good one,' and some say 'by measure,' like 'by measure' (Leviticus 19:35), and it is the straight." "<b>And barley.</b> Barley is known." "<b>Marked.</b> Like a sign." "<b>And the border of his boundary.</b> From the root of 'boundaries you shall make for it' (Exodus 28:14)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:42.707307585Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}